# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS FILE IS A DISCLOSURE CONTROL, NOT HOUSEKEEPING.
#
# The ARMS database holds 155 user accounts with e-mail addresses, telephone
# numbers, password hashes and nine South African ID numbers; 360 abattoir
# owner names and 586 telephone numbers; and eleven years of per-plant
# condemnation figures, which are commercially sensitive and are the reason the
# whole access-control layer exists.
#
# NONE OF IT BELONGS IN A GIT REPOSITORY, and a git repository does not forget.
# Anything committed here is recoverable from history even after it is deleted.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets. .env holds the SQL password.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Database backups and any extract of them.
*.bak
*.bacpac
*.dacpac
*.trn
*.mdf
*.ldf

# The BUILT explorer: 2,4 MB with every abattoir's figures and 529 telephone
# numbers compiled into it. app/explorer-template.html is the safe one - it is
# the same application with `var DATA = null`.
app/NAHDIS Explorer.html
NAHDIS Explorer.html

# The extracted payload behind it: owner names and contact numbers in `alias`.
nahdis-data.json
*-data.json

# Anything a person exported while looking at real figures.
*.xlsx
*.csv
!app/disease-name-map.csv
!.claude/**/*.csv

node_modules/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
